  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "important-chizuru-glossary-mechanics",
      "title": {
        "en": "Important Chizuru Glossary/Mechanics"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_1060_srt4",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_1060_uni1",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Karmic Flames is the most important skill for Chizuru\nKarmic Flames applies the permanent \"Cursed Shackles\" Debuff\nOnly ONE CURSED SHACKLE can exist at a time, among all enemies.\nCursed Shackled enemies either buff Karmic Flames (Unimportant)\nCursed Shackled enemies genererate \"Will o Wisp\" whenever they're hit\nAny ally, multi hits count multiple times, \"Extra Attacks\" do not count\n(Exception is from \"Bind\" Cards, currently only \"Shadow of the Moon\")\nEvery 5 Will o Wisp generated creates 1 Bind = 1 Shadow of the Moon\nThe other source of Will o Wisp is Tsukuyomi and its epiphanies\nMultiple copies merge Bind/Moon cards together, max stack is 5 Bind\n(Technically considered Created, before they're merged together)\nWhen \"Bind\" is stacked, the damage of Moon increases\nAt 3 Bind or more, Shadow of the Moon evolve into Shadow of the Moon+\nThe best damage comes from using Moon+ immediately when its created"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "To use, or not to use Bound at Dusk"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_1060_uni2",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Bound at Dusk gives Inhibit\nInhibit disables all AP sources besides for Start of Turn, or Ravage\nInhibit is technically a buff, so immunity doesn't work\nNo Fates, No Upgrades, No Divines, No Mika wave/source, nothing\nFor Chizuru specifically, if built well, ITS NOT A BIG ISSUE\nInhibit limits AP, but adds AP through its cost reduction mechanics\nBesides for the cost reductions/ap limitation\nInhibits only benefit is +1 Hit to Moon, or Moon+\nThis is not the biggest benefit in general, but the damage does stack up"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
